{"id":"a3","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":3,"of":10,"title":"One and many","titleHe":"יָחִיד וְרַבִּים","goal":"Form plurals, and recognise the irregular ones you'll use daily.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Masculine nouns take ־ִים, feminine nouns take ־וֹת. The vowels inside the word usually shorten when the ending is added."},{"type":"table","caption":"Regular plurals","head":["singular","plural"],"rows":[["סֵפֶר — book","סְפָרִים"],["יֶלֶד — boy","יְלָדִים"],["מוֹרָה — teacher (f.)","מוֹרוֹת"],["מִשְׁפָּחָה — family","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"The ending does not always match the gender. שֻׁלְחָן is masculine but pluralises שֻׁלְחָנוֹת; שָׁנָה is feminine but goes שָׁנִים. The gender doesn't change — only the ending is irregular."},{"type":"table","caption":"The irregulars worth memorising","head":["singular","plural"],"rows":[["אִישׁ — man","אֲנָשִׁים"],["אִשָּׁה — woman","נָשִׁים"],["בַּיִת — house","בָּתִּים"],["בֵּן — son","בָּנִים"],["בַּת — daughter","בָּנוֹת"],["שָׁנָה — year","שָׁנִים"]]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אִישׁ","en":"man","translit":"ish"},{"he":"אִשָּׁה","en":"woman","translit":"isha"},{"he":"אֲנָשִׁים","en":"people, men","translit":"anashim"},{"he":"נָשִׁים","en":"women","translit":"nashim"},{"he":"בָּתִּים","en":"houses","translit":"batim"},{"he":"סְפָרִים","en":"books","translit":"sfarim"},{"he":"יְלָדִים","en":"children","translit":"yeladim"},{"he":"שָׁנָה","en":"year","translit":"shana"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["man","wakes up","to her","there is, there are"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אִישׁ","translit":"ish"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["thus, so","knows, is acquainted with","teacher (m.)","woman"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אִשָּׁה","translit":"isha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["more, still, another","people, men","grandfather","very"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אֲנָשִׁים","translit":"anashim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["hard, difficult","give! (m.)","women","there isn't"],"correct":2,"prompt":"נָשִׁים","translit":"nashim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["time","houses","was (m.)","to me"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בָּתִּים","translit":"batim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["already","sees","strength","books"],"correct":3,"prompt":"סְפָרִים","translit":"sfarim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["went","with","word","children"],"correct":3,"prompt":"יְלָדִים","translit":"yeladim"},{"type":"choice","q":"Regular plurals — family?","options":["יְלָדִים","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת","סְפָרִים","מוֹרוֹת"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Regular plurals — book?","options":["סְפָרִים","מוֹרוֹת","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת","יְלָדִים"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “man”?","options":["הָיָה","גָּדוֹל","לָמָּה","אִישׁ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"The irregulars worth memorising — house?","options":["נָשִׁים","אֲנָשִׁים","בָּתִּים","בָּנִים"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"The irregulars worth memorising — year?","options":["נָשִׁים","שָׁנִים","בָּתִּים","אֲנָשִׁים"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"אֲנָשִׁים","translit":"anashim","en":"people, men"},{"type":"choice","q":"The irregulars worth memorising — man?","options":["בָּנִים","נָשִׁים","אֲנָשִׁים","בָּתִּים"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["סְפָרִים","יְלָדִים","אִישׁ","אִשָּׁה"],"correct":2,"say":"אִישׁ","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"What's the plural of אִשָּׁה?","options":["נָשִׁים","אִשּׁוֹת","אֲנָשִׁים","אִשִּׁים"],"correct":0,"why":"אִשָּׁה → נָשִׁים is irregular; אֲנָשִׁים is the plural of אִישׁ, man."}]}